+### Compound Format
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })      // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })          // "1s"
+```
+
+Compound output uses hours, minutes and seconds only (hours is the largest unit, so a day is `24h`), with no separators and zero parts skipped. Leftover milliseconds are dropped, so values under one second give `0s`. The output is compatible with Go's [`time.ParseDuration`](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration). `compound` takes precedence over `long`.
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
 ```ts
